  "implemented": [
    "Retained empty renderer arguments map to exact native empty payload; no clipboard target, URI, path, caller or permission can be chosen in public arguments. Node service receives no clipboard content or route.",
    "Native ingress requires trusted main label/origin, current engine epoch and opaque current physical-document authority. GTK requests and callback processing recheck the captured document before effects and delivery.",
    "Linux GTK target/content requests run asynchronously on the main thread. Target count is finite; fixed atoms avoid materializing arbitrary target names. Copied-file offers take priority and return a fixed message before content requests or filesystem effects.",
    "Empty/text clipboards return empty image/error arrays. Other known image formats return fixed unsupported wording. Non-Linux returns fixed unavailable wording.",
    "Successful output has one fixed-name PNG with canonical plain base64 and at most 512 KiB decoded bytes. Reported native length is checked before copying; strict codecs reject ambiguous envelopes, malformed base64, foreign fields and private diagnostics.",
    "Raw GTK callbacks remain retained under native work ownership despite timeout or dropped public waiters. Retired public requests cannot start subsequent content acquisition or copy bytes. Shutdown drains actual completion.",
    "Renderer hydration fences clipboard acquisition. Reload/disconnect reject pending results without replaying them into a replacement document."
  ],
